      },
      {
        "id": "parity-render-question",
        "role": "user",
        "content": "How can a Rust desktop show Markdown, code, formulas, and diagrams?",
        "timestamp": 1790848980000,
        "contentUpdatedAt": 1790848980000,
        "summary": "Render rich answers in Rust",
        "summaryTimestamp": 1790848980000
      },
      {
        "id": "parity-save-question",
        "role": "user",
        "content": "How can the desktop preserve edits when another window changes the project?",
        "timestamp": 1790849040000,
        "contentUpdatedAt": 1790849040000,
        "summary": "Preserve edits across conflicts",
        "summaryTimestamp": 1790849040000
      },
      {
        "id": "parity-render-answer",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "## Render the answer\n\nUse native text for **Markdown**, highlighted code, and tables. Render formulas and Mermaid into images in memory. Keep the exact Markdown available through Copy.\n\n```rust\nlet answer = RichText::new(markdown, cx);\n```\n\nThe interface remains a native desktop window.",
        "timestamp": 1790849100000,
        "contentUpdatedAt": 1790849100000,
        "summary": "Native Markdown, math, and diagrams",
        "summaryTimestamp": 1790849100000,
        "provider": "codex",
        "model": "fixture-codex"
      },
      {
        "id": "parity-save-answer",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "## Preserve the project\n\n1. Save with the revision that the window loaded.\n2. If the revision changed, keep the unsaved graph open.\n3. Compare both versions without replacing either.\n4. Save a separate copy or preserve a snapshot before reload.\n\nIndependent branches remain available while an answer streams.",
        "timestamp": 1790849160000,
        "contentUpdatedAt": 1790849160000,
        "summary": "Revision checks and recovery snapshots",
        "summaryTimestamp": 1790849160000,
        "provider": "claude-code",
        "model": "fixture-claude"
      },
      {
        "id": "parity-merge",
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Merge both branches into one desktop acceptance example. Keep the code, formula, table, diagram, and evidence visible.",
        "timestamp": 1790849220000,
        "contentUpdatedAt": 1790849220000,
        "summary": "Synthesize both branches",
        "summaryTimestamp": 1790849220000
      },
      {
        "id": "parity-synthesis",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "# A native desktop, one shared graph\n\nThis is **authored demonstration data**. It contains no live provider response.\n\n| Capability | Desktop behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Branches | Independent answers, shared ancestry |\n| Files | Vault references with bounded previews |\n| Saves | Revision checks and recovery snapshots |\n\n```rust\nlet ancestors = graph.conversation_path_ids(&node_id);\nlet response = render_markdown(answer);\nsave_with_revision(project, revision)?;\n```\n\nInline math: \\(E = mc^2\\). Display math:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i = \\bar{x}\n\\]\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[Native view] --> B[Shared Rust core]\n    B --> C[Saved project]\n```\n\n- [x] Preserve the answer text\n- [x] Keep provenance separate\n- [ ] Complete interactive acceptance checks\n\nThe two branches agree on these boundaries.【1】 A missing citation stays visible for inspection.【9】\n",
        "timestamp": 1790849280000,
        "contentUpdatedAt": 1790849280000,
        "summary": "Native rich answer and evidence",
        "summaryTimestamp": 1790849280000,
